# Reactive Animation Constraint System (Public Edition)

This experimental concept describes how reactive animation could function without revealing implementation specifics.

## Purpose
Enable procedural animation that respects physical limits while reacting to gameplay. Engineering task lists, anatomical datasets, and tuning constants are **[REDACTED]**.

## Codex Responsibilities
- Define reusable motion stencils and action templates at a conceptual level.
- Outline how entropy modulates movement without exceeding safe bounds.
Detailed data structures, binding maps, and integration scripts are **[REDACTED]**.

## Runtime Responsibilities
Engines should observe events, apply appropriate stencils, and trigger fallbacks when chaos output misbehaves. Source code, performance captures, and debugging utilities are **[REDACTED]**.

## Constraint Enforcement
The system maintains joint limits and routes invalid states to deterministic animations. Threshold tables, logging conventions, and override policies are **[REDACTED]**.

## Use Cases
Examples include reactive limb motion, controlled destruction, and fluid responses. Numerical ranges, particle presets, and safety drills are **[REDACTED]**.

## Summary
Think of RACS as a blueprint for future work. Consult the protected repository for executable specifications and ongoing experiments.
